  "plain": "In 1996, in the Brazilian town of Varginha, a story spread that a strange creature had been captured and that a young military policeman who helped catch it later died. A podcast host, Jesse Michels, says he interviewed the doctor who did the autopsy on that soldier, a man he calls Armando Fortunato. Michels names the soldier as Marco Chereze. He says Chereze seemed to die of a bacterial infection unlike anything seen before, and that he was likely hurt by a being from another world. The doctor himself tells it more carefully. He says that when the soldier's body came to the Forensic Medical Institute, nobody mentioned any contact with extraterrestrials. He says the autopsy was ordered to check whether another doctor had made a professional mistake. So the host and the doctor are the two voices here, one framing it as an alien story and the other recalling a routine inquiry, and if the host is right, a man died from touching a living alien."
}
